1.25.0

Added: tenants and their services can be managed: New-, Update-, Enable-, Disable-, Remove- and
Restore-PmTenant, and Add-, Remove-, Enable- and Disable-PmTenantService, with
Get-PmAvailableService. The cmdlets wait for the asynchronous operation to finish (-NoWait returns).

Added: Copy-Item copies a folder under a new name, as on the file system. Get-OrchTaskData reads a
task's form values and the action it was completed with.

Changed: *-OrchActionCatalog are renamed *-OrchTaskCatalog; the former names still work once the
module is loaded. Tasks come in Action Center's order. Get-OrchLicenseRuntime shows IsLicensed as
True / False.

Fixed: a copy whose reference lookup fails (403 for a missing scope, a network error) no longer
creates the entity without it -- Copy-OrchTrigger created a trigger without its executor robots,
which once enabled runs on any robot in the folder; an asset lost its per-user values. That entity
is now skipped with an error naming the lookup; a reference the destination does not have is a
warning, as before.

Fixed: New-/Update- cmdlets (triggers, API triggers, queues, processes, test set schedules,
machines) skip an entity when a name they were given does not resolve, instead of creating or
changing it without that name: a failed -QueueDefinitionName made a time trigger, enabled and
running every minute by default.

Fixed: Get-OrchTask finds modern-folder tasks; Remove-OrchTask removes a task.

Fixed: the help of Copy-OrchTrigger and New-OrchTrigger lists the OAuth scopes they need.

1.24.0

Added: Copy-Item Tm1:\PRJ Tm2:\[NEWPREFIX] copies a whole Test Manager project, also to another
tenant: requirements, test cases with their steps, test sets, their labels and assignments, and
the time zone and execution name format. Copy-TmTestCase, Copy-TmRequirement and Copy-TmTestSet
copy the items whose names match. Items are matched with the destination's by name and foreign
reference, so running a copy again adds nothing; items that cannot be matched one-to-one are
skipped with a warning, and -Force creates them.

Added: Get-PmOrganization, Get-PmTenant and Get-PmTenantService read the organization, its
tenants and each tenant's services (orchestrator, testmanager, ...) with their status and URL.
Automation Cloud and Automation Suite.

Added: Get-TmTestSetTestCase and Get-TmRequirementTestCase output the test case's
foreignReference.

1.23.0

Added: Test Manager can be written to, not only read and removed. New-Item Tm:\PREFIX creates a
project. New- and Update-TmRequirement, -TmTestCase and -TmTestSet create and change requirements,
test cases and test sets. Get-, New-, Update-, Move- and Remove-TmTestStep work on manual test
steps. Get-, Add- and Remove-TmTestSetTestCase and -TmRequirementTestCase assign test cases to
test sets and requirements.

Added: -ExportCsv on Get-TmRequirement, Get-TmTestCase, Get-TmTestSet, Get-TmTestStep,
Get-TmTestSetTestCase and Get-TmRequirementTestCase. The file pipes back through Import-Csv into
the matching New- or Add- cmdlet in another project or tenant, labels included.

Fixed: Copy-Item -Recurse into a destination folder that already exists no longer skips
triggers, and what it copies shows up in Get-Orch* at once, without Clear-OrchCache.

Fixed: Copy-Item -Recurse and Copy-OrchActionCatalog wait for a folder just created before
copying action catalogs into it, instead of failing.

Fixed: Clear-OrchCache Orch1:\ -Recurse (or -Depth) clears the folders' caches too.

Fixed: progress text hides only the characters the console would mis-size.

1.22.0

Fixed: Copy-OrchQueueItem reads the source queue in order of Id. It paged through the New items
in an order that was not fixed (EndProcessing, empty on every New item), so a queue of more than
100 items could have items copied twice or not at all. It also copies SpecificContent as it was
added: a date-time string is no longer converted to UTC, and value types are kept.

Fixed: Add-PmUserLicense resolves -License against the licenses the organisation holds, so App
Testing bundles such as APPTESTDEVNU can be assigned; a name given in full that matches nothing
is now an error. Remove-PmGroupLicense accepts a raw bundle code. Remove-PmGroup removes the
group's licensing record too (Automation Cloud and Automation Suite).

Fixed: piping users from Get-PmUser (or its CSV) into Copy-, Update-, Remove- or Get-PmUser works
for users without an email. The parameter is now -UserName with the alias -Email; both names and
the positional form keep working.

Added: an Entitlements column on Get-PmUserLicense, Get-PmGroupLicense and Get-PmLicenseInventory;
bundle names filled in on Get-PmLicenseInventory; Remove-PmLicensedGroup -Id for orphan rows.

Help: the Migration Guide says what a copy leaves in place of passwords (!!!PLEASE UPDATE!!!), and
the scope lists are corrected (OR.Roles does not exist; OR.Settings.Read where the credential
store is looked up).

1.21.1

Removed: Import-OrchQueueItem -IncludeProcessedItems (added in 1.21.0). It created the rows as New,
which its name did not say. To queue finished items again, remove the @Status column from the
exported file (or set a row's @Status to New) and import it.

Fixed: Import-OrchQueueItem reads the web's Deadline and Postpone columns (the item's due and
postpone dates) as the web does; they were stored as SpecificContent. Get-OrchQueueItem -ExportCsv
writes them in place of @DueDate/@DeferDate, so moved items keep their dates, and writes nothing
for a queue whose read failed part-way instead of a file that looks complete.

1.21.0

Added: Get-OrchQueueItem -ExportCsv writes queue items in any status to CSV, one file per queue: the
web Upload Items columns (Reference, Priority, one column per SpecificContent key) followed by the
item's history in '@' columns (@Status, @Output, @Robot, processing times, ...). Import-OrchQueueItem
reads such a file back, keeps the '@' columns out of SpecificContent and imports only the New rows
unless -IncludeProcessedItems is given.

Added: Import-OrchQueueItem -DynamicTyping, as the web's Dynamic typing check box (two web defects
not reproduced), and delimiter detection (comma, tab, |, ;).

Changed: Import-OrchQueueItem was checked file by file against the web Upload Items. It sends 1,000
rows per request (AllOrNothing stays one request) and reports the rows sent and not sent if a request
fails; rejects rows with fewer fields than the header, as Import-OrchTestDataQueueItem now does too;
renames repeated column names as the web does; accepts a single-column CSV.

Fixed: line breaks inside quoted values are kept as written; spaces around a Priority value are
ignored; CSV error row numbers no longer shift after a rejected row; a large BulkAddQueueItems request
waits up to 30 minutes instead of 100 seconds; Remove-OrchQueueItem -Id with many ids looks them up
100 per request instead of one by one.

1.20.0

Added: Wait-OrchJob waits until jobs end, and Start-OrchJob -Wait starts and waits. Jobs come from
the pipeline, -Id or -BatchExecutionKey; -Timeout leaves the jobs still running as errors.

Added: Measure-OrchLog counts robot logs per folder with Get-OrchLog's filters, without fetching
them and without the 10,000 cap of @odata.count on Automation Cloud.

Added: Find-OrchAccountReference finds where a Windows account is used -- users, robots,
credential assets, per-user asset values and the triggers on a matched user's robot -- for
example before its password changes.

Added: a user mapping CSV moves a tenant's users onto other users of the same tenant, for a domain
change or a switch of identity provider (New-OrchUserMappingCsv -SourceDomain/-DestinationDomain,
then Copy-OrchUser and Copy-OrchFolderUser within one tenant).

Added: New-PmExternalApplication registers an external application; Test-PmExternalApplication
reviews registrations (secrets, scopes, redirect URLs) and tests a client-credentials sign-in.

Added: Start-OrchJob sets the Start Job dialog's options (-Priority, -StopStrategy, stop, kill and
alert times). The sign-in page names the server's edition and version, and a Scope refused for its
length says so with the server's limit.

Changed: the API version is read from /api/Status/Version, so OR.Settings is no longer needed or
warned about at mount. API triggers and Secret assets follow each server's web UI. License cmdlets
skip robot types an older server lacks. A 401 re-sign-in tries the refresh token before the browser.

Fixed: Get-OrchLog reads past 10,000 logs on Automation Cloud; -Machine and -WindowsIdentity with a
name that matches nothing return no logs, and -Machine finds machines not assigned to the folder.
Copy-OrchFolderUser -UserMappingCsv keeps the roles of a user already in the folder. Start-OrchJob
starts one job on 20.10 to 22.10. Two on-premises drives no longer share organization data.
Get-OrchFolderMachineAccountMapping works on 22.10 and later. Copy-Item copies test data queues on
standalone 24.10 and 25.10. Platform Management list cmdlets carry on past a drive without the
feature.

1.19.1

Fixed: triggers keep their robot assignment on on-premises servers and Automation Suite. 1.19.0
read it from an expanded trigger listing that only Automation Cloud fills, so there
Get-OrchTriggerDetail showed no robots, -ExportCsv wrote none and Copy-Item copied triggers without
them. Get-OrchTriggerDetail is back to one request per trigger.

Fixed: Update-OrchTrigger no longer clears a trigger's robot assignment, which any update did since
1.0.0.

Fixed: a 401 from a service other than Orchestrator (Identity, for the Pm cmdlets on 20.10) no
longer makes the whole drive fail until Import-OrchConfig.

Fixed: copying the same process twice in a session keeps its entry point.

Fixed on 20.10: exported trigger rows name their robots; a trigger priority is sent as Low / Normal
/ High; Copy-Item copies local-account folder users; Add-OrchFolderUser -Type User / Robot assigns
local accounts.

Changed: Get-OrchProcessDetail reads entry point paths from the listing, one request fewer per
process; Get-OrchTestSetDetail prints each folder as it arrives.
